### One Quick Upgrade: The `&&` (AND) Operator

Your nested `if` statements work perfectly, but JavaScript has a shortcut built exactly for this situation so you don't have to write an `if` inside an `if`. 

You can use the logical **`&&`** operator to check both conditions at the exact same time on a single line:

```javascript
// This reads: If userInput is 'admin' AND passwordInput is '1234'
if (userInput === 'admin' && passwordInput === '1234') {
    wrongCredentials.textContent = "Login Successful!";
    wrongCredentials.style.color = "green";
} else {
    wrongCredentials.textContent = "Invalid Credentials";
    wrongCredentials.style.color = "red";
}
```

Using `&&` keeps your code clean and handles all the "wrong" cases (wrong username, wrong password, or both wrong) under that single, elegant `else` block. 

