        //    - Grab what the user typed inside the textarea using .value
        //    - Create a brand new 'li' element using document.createElement('li')
        //    - Set the .textContent of that new 'li' to match the user's typed text.
        //    - Append that new 'li' to your list using container.appendChild(newLi)
        //    - Clear the textarea by setting its value back to an empty string: input.value = "";

    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

