### üö® Think Hard: The Architectural Trap

Before you type a single line, you are going to hit a major logical roadblock that separates beginner coders from structural engineers. 

When you use `querySelectorAll('.del-btn')` at the very top of your script page, **it will only find elements that exist when the page first loads.** It will *not* automatically attach listeners to new items you create later on. 

How are you going to ensure that every brand-new task you build dynamically gets a working delete button attached to it? 

