### üèÜ The Final Boss: The Gamified Goal Tracker

You are building an app where a user tracks a daily goal (like "Drink 4 Liters of Water" or "Study for 2 hours"). 

Every time they hit a `+` button, their progress goes up. If they hit a `-` button, it goes down. But here is the twist: **The UI must dynamically change based on their progress.**



---

### üß† The Mission Specifications

Copy this code into a new file. You need to write the script to handle these features:

1. **The Increments:** Clicking the `+` button increases the count by 1. Clicking `-` decreases it by 1 (but it can never go below 0!).
2. **The Goal Threshold:** The target goal is **10**. 
3. **The State Change (The Hard Part):** * If progress is between **1 and 9**, the status text must say `"Keep pushing! You're on your way."` and the card background should stay dark.
   * If progress hits **10 or more**, the status text must change to `"Target Achieved! Mission Complete! üöÄ"`, the text color of the number should turn neon green, and the target progress text should update.

---

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Goal Tracker Arena</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #0b0f19;
            color: #ffffff;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
        }
        .tracker-card {
            background: #171e30;
            padding: 40px;
            border-radius: 20px;
            width: 320px;
            text-align: center;
            box-shadow: 0 15px 35px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
            border: 2px solid #252f48;
            transition: all 0.3s ease;
        }
        h2 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #a5b4fc; }
        
        /* The Number Display */
        #score-display {
            font-size: 72px;
            font-weight: bold;
            margin: 20px 0;
            color: #ffffff;
            transition: color 0.3s;
        }
        
        /* Control Buttons */
        .btn-group {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 25px;
        }
        button {
            width: 60px;
            height: 60px;
            border-radius: 50%;
            border: none;
            font-size: 28px;
            font-weight: bold;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: transform 0.1s, background 0.2s;
        }
        #minus-btn { background-color: #ef4444; color: white; }
        #minus-btn:hover { background-color: #dc2626; }
        #plus-btn { background-color: #10b981; color: white; }
        #plus-btn:hover { background-color: #059669; }
        button:active { transform: scale(0.9); }

        /* Dynamic Feedback Text */
        #status-msg {
            font-size: 14px;
            color: #94a3b8;
            min-height: 40px;
            line-height: 1.4;
        }

        /* Target indicator */
        .target-tag {
            font-size: 12px;
            background: #252f48;
            padding: 4px 12px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            color: #6366f1;
            display: inline-block;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        /* CSS Helper Classes for your JS to utilize */
        .victory-text { color: #10b981 !important; text-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(16,185,129,0.4); }
        .victory-card { border-color: #10b981; box-shadow: 0 15px 35px rgba(16,185,129,0.2); }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="tracker-card" id="main-card">
        <span class="target-tag">TARGET: 10</span>
        <h2>Daily Mission</h2>
        
        <div id="score-display">0</div>

        <div class="btn-group">
            <button id="minus-btn">-</button>
            <button id="plus-btn">+</button>
        </div>

        <p id="status-msg">Click buttons to start tracking progress.</p>
    </div>

    <script>
        // WRITE YOUR CODE HERE
        // 1. Target the elements (#score-display, #minus-btn, #plus-btn, #status-msg, #main-card)
        // 2. Keep track of the live score using a counter variable in memory.
        // 3. Set up event listeners for BOTH buttons.
        // 4. Implement conditional logic (if / else) to check the score value after every click.
        //    Hint: To add a class to an element, use element.classList.add("classname")
        //    Hint: To remove a class, use element.classList.remove("classname")
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

