The trap with the score change logic is making sure you change the text content **and** handle the CSS visual updates at the exact same moment. 

Here is exactly how you handle the `+` button step-by-step:

```javascript
// 1. Keep track of the number in memory (Outside the listener)
let currentScore = 0;

plusButton.addEventListener("click", function() {
    // 2. Increase the memory count
    currentScore += 1;
    
    // 3. Update the number on the screen instantly
    scoreDisplay.textContent = currentScore;
    
    // 4. THE CONDITIONAL CHECK: Read the new number
    if (currentScore >= 10) {
        statusMsg.textContent = "Target Achieved! Mission Complete! üöÄ";
        
        // Apply the neon glow classes from the CSS panel
        scoreDisplay.classList.add("victory-text");
        mainCard.classList.add("victory-card");
    } else {
        statusMsg.textContent = "Keep pushing! You're on your way.";
    }
});
```

