However, your code has **two bugs** that will stop it from working completely‚Äîone is a minor typo, and the other is a deep **Variable Scope Trap**.

Let‚Äôs break them down so you can fix them.

---

### 1. The Typo Bug üî§
```javascript
let statusMessage = document.quertSelector("#status-msg");
```
* **The Error:** You typed `quertSelector` with a `t` instead of a `y`. JavaScript will crash on page load saying `document.quertSelector is not a function`. Change that `t` to a `y`!

---

### 2. The Scope Trap (The Big One) üõë
Look at where you read and updated the score:
```javascript
// OUTSIDE the event listener
let scoreInNum = scoreDisplay.textContent;
let finalScore = Number(scoreInNum);

plusButton.addEventListener("click", function(){
    finalScore += 1;
    scoreDisplay.textContent = finalScore;
})
```

Your calculation logic is correct, but there is a hidden flaw. What if you want to click the `minusButton` next? Because `finalScore` was created outside of any specific button, it works fine for the plus button, but you haven't handled the conditional checks inside the click yet.

If you don't look at the numbers **inside** the click event listener, your app won't know when to fire the if/else statements for the victory badges.

---

### üõ†Ô∏è The Fix & Next Steps

Update your `<script>` block to look like this. I have fixed your typo and left comments showing exactly where to drop your `if/else` checks:

```javascript
let mainCard = document.querySelector("#main-card");
let scoreDisplay = document.querySelector("#score-display");
let minusButton = document.querySelector("#minus-btn");
let plusButton = document.querySelector("#plus-btn");
let statusMessage = document.querySelector("#status-msg"); // Typo fixed!

// This variable tracks the score in memory
let finalScore = 0; 

plusButton.addEventListener("click", function(){
    finalScore += 1;
    scoreDisplay.textContent = finalScore;

    // üëá ADD YOUR IF/ELSE LOGIC FOR THE PLUS BUTTON HERE üëá
    // If finalScore is 10 or more:
    //    - Change statusMessage text
    //    - Add "victory-text" class to scoreDisplay
    //    - Add "victory-card" class to mainCard
    // Else:
    //    - Set statusMessage to "Keep pushing! You're on your way."
})   

minusButton.addEventListener("click", function(){
    // üëá WRITE YOUR MINUS BUTTON LOGIC HERE üëá
    // 1. Decrease finalScore by 1 (But wrap it so it can't go below 0!)
    // 2. Update scoreDisplay text
    // 3. Add an if/else check here too: If it drops below 10, REMOVE the victory classes!
})
```

