yWell i got a question where should i input survive in the input section or the new element where we created and added it ïThat is an excellent question. You need to handle the "survival" logic inside the **new element section (Phase 2)**, completely separate from the input fields. 

Think of it like this: when the user hits refresh, the page completely wipes itself clean. The text input fields will be empty, and the list on the screen will be gone. 

The only things that survive the refresh are the values inside `localStorage`. 

Your goal during the `window.addEventListener("load", ...)` phase is to grab those surviving text values directly from the vault and construct a brand-new list element from scratch right onto the screen.

---

### üó∫Ô∏è The Architecture of Survival

Here is exactly how the process flows when the page reloads:



---

### üõ†Ô∏è How to write Phase 2

Inside your `load` event listener, your code should look like this. You aren't touching the input fields at all; you are reading from storage and printing directly to the list:

```javascript
window.addEventListener("load", function() {
    // 1. Peek inside the storage vault
    let savedName = localStorage.getItem("latestName");
    let savedScore = localStorage.getItem("latestScore");

    // 2. CHECK: If there is actually data inside the vault, rebuild the item!
    if (savedName && savedScore) {
        let newList = document.createElement("li");
        let span = document.createElement("span");
        let sspan = document.createElement("span");

        // 3. Populate the tags with the SURVIVED data
        span.textContent = savedName;
        sspan.textContent = savedScore;
        sspan.classList.add("score-val");

        // 4. Throw it onto the screen instantly on boot
        newList.appendChild(span);
        newList.appendChild(sspan);
        scoreList.appendChild(newList);
    }
});
```

### üßπ Phase 3: The Wipe Button
To round out the app, your clear button just needs to do the exact opposite. It destroys the vault data and clears the screen visual:

```javascript
clearBtn.addEventListener("click", function() {
    localStorage.clear();   // Clears the hard drive vault
    scoreList.innerHTML = ""; // Rips all items off the screen visuals
});
```

