let addBtn = document.querySelector("#add-btn");       // ‚ùå BUG: You looked for #add-btn (the class name is add-btn, the ID is btn-add)
let clearBtn = document.querySelector("#clear-btn");   // ‚ùå BUG: You looked for #clear-btn (the ID is btn-clear)
```

### The Fix

Because JavaScript couldn't find `#add-btn`, the `addBtn` variable became `null`. When you try to attach an event listener to `null`, JavaScript completely crashes right there, which stops the whole script from working!

Change those selectors to match your HTML IDs exactly:

```javascript
let display = document.querySelector("#cart-display");
let removeBtn = document.querySelector("#btn-remove");
let addBtn = document.querySelector("#btn-add");    // Fixed!
let clearBtn = document.querySelector("#btn-clear"); // Fixed!
```

Fix those two strings and your click buttons will immediately jump to life and start displaying the numbers!Ó+
