</html> can you just highlight me the one error on refreshing i dont know its getting reset ’You are incredibly close! Your event handlers are beautifully wired, your elements are selected correctly now, and your clear button logic is flawless. 

The reason it is resetting on a refresh is due to how you are talking to `localStorage`. You made a mistake with **Keys vs. Values**.

---

### üö® The Refresh Bug: Missing the Key Name

When you call `localStorage.setItem()`, the vault demands **two things**: a label/key name (a string text) so it knows where to file it, and the actual value you want to save. 

Look at your code inside the click buttons:
```javascript
localStorage.setItem(cartCount); // ‚ùå Error! You only provided the value.
```
Because there is no label name, the browser doesn't know how to track it.

Then look at your window `load` listener:
```javascript
let getValue = localStorage.getItem(cartCount); // ‚ùå Error! You are passing a changing number variable as the key name.
```

When the page loads, `cartCount` is `0`. So your code asks the vault: *"Hey, give me whatever is saved under the name `0`."* But nothing is named `0` inside the vault, so `getValue` becomes empty (`null`). Your screen then overwrites the `0` with absolute nothingness!

---

### üõ†Ô∏è The Absolute Fix

You need to pick **one permanent text name** (a key string) and use it consistently for saving, reading, and loading. Let's call it `"savedCartTotal"`.

Update those specific lines in your script:

#### 1. Inside `removeBtn` and `addBtn`:
```javascript
// Give the value a proper text label/key name!
localStorage.setItem("savedCartTotal", cartCount);
```

#### 2. Inside `window.load`:
```javascript
window.addEventListener("load", function() {
    // Look up the exact text label we saved it under
    let getValue = localStorage.getItem("savedCartTotal");
    
    // CRITICAL FIX: Only update if something actually exists in the vault!
    if (getValue !== null) {
        cartCount = Number(getValue); // Sync your memory variable with the vault
        display.textContent = cartCount; // Render it to the screen
    }
});
```

### üí° Why syncing `cartCount = Number(getValue)` matters:
If you don't update your `cartCount` tracking variable back to the saved number on load, your memory variable stays at `0`. Then, if the user reloads with 5 items in their cart and clicks `+`, your memory variable goes from `0` to `1` instead of jumping from `5` to `6`!

Swap those `localStorage` lines to use the `"savedCartTotal"` string key, and your cart survival engine will be 100% unbreakable!†/
