### üöÄ The Next Frontier: The Dynamic Task Matrix

In your previous apps, you could only track a single number or a single player string. If you added something new, the old data was overwritten. Real-world applications manage collections of data using **Arrays** and **Objects**.

Your next challenge is to build a **Persistent Task Matrix (To-Do Tracker)**. 

Instead of saving a single variable, your code will manage a master database array containing multiple independent task records:
```javascript
let taskList = [
    { id: 1, text: "Master JavaScript Arrays", completed: false },
    { id: 2, text: "Learn JSON Stringify", completed: true }
];
```

---

### üõ†Ô∏è The New Core Mechanics You Will Master

To make an entire array survive a browser refresh, you have to use two legendary text-transformation utilities because `localStorage` only stores flat strings:

1. **`JSON.stringify(yourArray)`**: This smashes your structured JavaScript array/objects into a single flat string of text so you can slip it into the `localStorage` vault.
2. **`JSON.parse(yourSavedString)`**: This takes that flat text string back out of the vault on page load and resurrects it back into a fully operational JavaScript array.

---

### ‚öîÔ∏è The Blueprint Arena

Copy this code into a fresh file. The layout and styling are already locked down. Your job is to step into the blank `<script>` tag and build the array management machine.

```html
