Hfor (let i = 0; i < movies.length; i++) {
    console.log(movies[i]); 
}„Spot on! Your fingers have officially mastered the syntax. That loop is flawless. It starts at `0`, stops exactly when the train ends, and uses the counter `i` to look inside each car one by one.

Now you have the three ultimate array superpowers in your toolbox:
1. `.push()` to add items.
2. `.length` to count items.
3. The `for` loop to step through every item.

Let's immediately plug these superpowers into your HTML screen layout so you can see why arrays are so incredibly useful.

---

### üé® Connecting the Array to the Visual Screen

Go back to your **Task Matrix Arena** file. We want to write a function that takes whatever is sitting inside your array train and builds it onto your monitor screen as physical list items (`<li>`).

We call this a **Render Engine**. Here is how we write it:

```javascript
function renderMatrix() {
    // 1. Clear out the old visual list entirely so we don't accidentally double-print items!
    matrixList.innerHTML = "";

    // 2. RUN YOUR FLUSH NEW LOOP! 
    // We step through your operationalTasks array car by car
    for (let i = 0; i < operationalTasks.length; i++) {
        
        // 3. Create the HTML elements out of thin air
        let newLi = document.createElement("li");
        let taskSpan = document.createElement("span");

        // 4. Fill the text content with the string inside the current array car!
        taskSpan.textContent = operationalTasks[i];

        // 5. Throw it onto the screen visuals
        newLi.appendChild(taskSpan);
        matrixList.appendChild(newLi);
    }
}
```



---

### üéÆ Putting It All Together (No Storage Vault Yet!)

Let's wire this up to your "Deploy" button. Open your file and update your script tag to look exactly like this. We are leaving the `localStorage` vault out for now so you can just watch the array and the rendering engine work:

```javascript
let taskInput = document.querySelector("#task-input");
let addTaskBtn = document.querySelector("#add-task-btn");
let matrixList = document.querySelector("#matrix-list");

// Our empty master array train
let operationalTasks = [];

addTaskBtn.addEventListener("click", function() {
    let taskText = taskInput.value;
    if (taskText === "") return; // Stop if nothing was typed

    // 1. Add the text to our array train
    operationalTasks.push(taskText);

    // 2. Clear out the input field
    taskInput.value = "";

    // 3. Fire up the engine to update our screen visuals!
    renderMatrix();
});

// The Render Engine Function
function renderMatrix() {
    matrixList.innerHTML = ""; // Wipe the old screen visual clear

    for (let i = 0; i < operationalTasks.length; i++) {
        let newLi = document.createElement("li");
        let taskSpan = document.createElement("span");

        taskSpan.textContent = operationalTasks[i]; // Insert data from array car 'i'

        newLi.appendChild(taskSpan);
        matrixList.appendChild(newLi);
    }
}
```

