```

**Your Objective:** Write a few lines of code to isolate the string `"google"` dynamically and store it inside a variable named `companyName`.



#### üó∫Ô∏è The Step-by-Step Blueprint to Follow:
1. Use `.split()` on the `email` variable to chop it at the `"@"` symbol. This will give you an array with two pieces: `["alex.jones", "google.com"]`. Save this array into a temporary variable.
2. Grab the second piece of that array (index `1`, which is `"google.com"`).
3. Use `.split()` *again*, but this time chop it at the dot (`"."`) symbol! This will give you another array: `["google", "com"]`.
4. Grab index `0` of that final array, which is exactly `"google"`, and assign it to `companyName`.
5. `console.log(companyName)` to make sure it prints perfectly!

