### ü™ì The 10 Punishment Specifications

Write all your solution logic inside the `<script>` tag at the bottom of the sandbox file. **Use arrow functions and modern ES6+ syntax wherever possible.**

#### ‚öîÔ∏è Level 1: Core Selection & HTML Injection
1. **The Urgent Alert Generator:** Target `#alert-btn` and `#alert-box`. When the button is clicked, inject a full custom HTML string into the alert box using `.innerHTML` containing an `<h1>‚ö†Ô∏è CRITICAL ERROR</h1>`.
2. **The Text Minimizer:** Target `#minimize-btn` and `#promo-text`. When clicked, take the existing text content, lowercase it entirely (`.toLowerCase()`), and update the text content to show the result.
3. **The Live Character Counter:** Target `#tweet-input` and `#char-count`. Add an `"input"` event listener to the input box. Every time a user types, update the text content of `#char-count` with the current string length (`.length`) of the input.

#### ‚öîÔ∏è Level 2: Modern Mapping & List Iteration
4. **The VIP Gateway List:** You have an array: `const users = ["alex", "sam", "jordan"];`. Target `#vip-btn` and `#vip-list`. When clicked, use `.map()` to transform each user into a string like `<li>VIP: [Name]</li>`, and assign the completely mapped array block to the container's `.innerHTML` (Hint: you can use `.join("")` on the mapped array result to glue them into one string!).
5. **The Dynamic Incrementor List:** Target `#add-num-btn` and `#num-list`. Create a global variable counter starting at 1. Every time the button is clicked, create a new `<li>` element out of thin air, set its text to show that counter, append it to `#num-list`, and increment the global counter variable.
6. **The Inventory Price Multiplier:** Target `#inflation-btn` and *all* spans matching `.price` (using `querySelectorAll`). When clicked, loop through the elements using `.forEach()`. Extract their text content, convert it to a number, multiply it by `2`, and write it right back to the screen.

#### ‚öîÔ∏è Level 3: Advanced Architecture & Destruction
7. **The Modern Template Welcomer:** Target `#user-name`, `#welcome-btn`, and `#welcome-output`. When clicked, read the input's value, and write a greeting message to `#welcome-output` using a **Template Literal backtick string**.
8. **The Modern Object Unpacker:** Given the object `const server = { ip: "192.168.1.1", status: "online", load: "12%" };`. Target `#unpack-btn` and `#specs-output`. When clicked, use **Object Destructuring** to unpack `ip` and `status` in a single line, then display them cleanly in the output paragraph.
9. **The Self-Destructing Node:** Target `#spawn-btn` and `#node-container`. When clicked, dynamically create a brand-new button element with a class `.badge` and text `"Boom! Click to delete me"`. Before appending it inside `#node-container`, attach a click handler *directly to it* that calls its own `.remove()` instruction.
10. **The Master Task Striker:** Target all elements with class `.task-check`. Use `.forEach()` to loop through them and attach a `"change"` event listener to every checkbox. Inside the listener, write conditional logic: if the checkbox is checked (`checkboxElement.checked === true`), add a CSS property directly to its parent element (`.parentElement.style.textDecoration = "line-through"`), otherwise clear it!

