## üí° One Quick Trick for "Compiling" Your Thoughts

When you sit down to look at a problem and your brain starts to freeze up, **step away from the keyboard and write pseudo-code (plain English) first.** Instead of trying to type JavaScript immediately, write down a checklist of steps like a cooking recipe:

```markdown
// 1. Get the button from the HTML page.
// 2. Listen for a click on that button.
// 3. When clicked, look at the input value.
// 4. IF the value is blank, stop right here.
// 5. ELSE, change the text on the screen.
```

Once your recipe is written in plain English, your only job is to translate those lines *one by one* into JavaScript code. It takes the pressure off trying to remember everything at once!

Take a breather, check out one of those sites, and practice at Level 1 for a bit. You've already made massive progress today‚Äîbe proud of how far you've come!õ
