†well i had a small doubt help me elaborate and clear my doubt about in minimum words do i need to know about DOM manipulation if i opt for software development ≠Yes. If you build anything that a user touches on a browser screen, you must understand DOM manipulation.

Here is why:

### 1. Modern Frameworks Are Built on It
Whether you use raw JavaScript now or move to advanced full-stack frontend frameworks like **React, Vue, or Next.js** later, they all do the exact same thing under the hood. They take database data and dynamically manipulate the browser's DOM nodes to change what is on the screen. 



### 2. The Full-Stack Pipeline
In software engineering, a web application is fundamentally a data highway:
$$\text{Database (Phase 4)} \longrightarrow \text{Server API (Phase 3)} \longrightarrow \text{DOM Manipulation (Phase 1)} \longrightarrow \text{User Screen}$$

If you do not understand how data alters the DOM, you cannot connect your backend databases to a real, working user interface. 

