## üìà Problem 38: The Social Media Notification Center

**The Scenario:** You are building an interactive notification feed for a social media platform. Users need to be able to click a "Mark as Read" button on each notification. Clicking it should toggle its visual style and dynamically update an unread counter at the top of the screen.

### 1. The HTML Structure
```html
<div class="notification-panel">
    <h2>Unread Alerts: <span id="unread-count">3</span></h2>
    
    <div id="feed-wrapper"></div>
</div>
```

### 2. The JavaScript Data Array
```javascript
const userNotifications = [
  { id: 1, text: "Elena liked your comment.", isRead: false },
  { id: 2, text: "Marcus sent you a friend request.", isRead: false },
  { id: 3, text: "Your order #8841 has shipped.", isRead: false }
];
```

### 3. Your Task
Write the JavaScript logic to hook this entire system up:

* **The Global Setup:**
  * Target your main feed container: `#feed-wrapper`.
  * Target your counter text element: `#unread-count`.
  * Create a mutable tracking variable called `unreadTotal` and initialize it to the length of the array (`userNotifications.length`).
* **The Loop & Component Build:**
  * Loop through `userNotifications`.
  * Dynamically create a `div` parent card with the class `"notification-card"`.
  * Set its `.innerHTML` to contain the notification text string and a button: `<p>${...}</p> <button class="read-btn">Mark as Read</button>`.
* **The Interactivity Rule:**
  * Find the specific button (`.read-btn`) inside your created card element using `.querySelector()`.
  * Add a `"click"` event listener to that button.
  * **The Toggle Logic:** When the button is clicked:
    1. Change the parent card's background color property to a faded grey (`"#f3f4f6"`).
    2. Disable the button so it can't be clicked again by setting its disabled property to true: `yourButtonVariable.disabled = true;`
    3. Decrease your `unreadTotal` variable by $1$ ($unreadTotal = unreadTotal - 1$).
    4. Update the text content of your counter element (`#unread-count`) to show the brand new `unreadTotal` number!
* **The Finale:** Append the completed card cleanly inside your feed wrapper container.

