```

### 2. The JavaScript Data Array
```javascript
const warehouseStock = [
  { sku: "SKU-99", name: "Mechanical Keyboard", stock: 4 },
  { sku: "SKU-42", name: "Ultrawide Monitor", stock: 2 }
];
```

### 3. The Requirement
You must write the code that renders these products onto the screen. Each product element must have an internal button labeled `"Purchase"`. 

Every time a user clicks that specific button, it must decrement that specific product's stock number on the screen by $1$. If the stock level for that product hits exactly $0$, the purchase button must immediately become disabled and its text must change to say `"Out of Stock"`. 

