### üîç The Fix
The requirement stated that if listeners are **greater than 0**, you must **remove** the empty class, and if it **is 0**, you **add** it. Since clicking the button *adds* $1$ to the listener count, the total can never drop to zero upon a click‚Äîit can only go up.

Here is the corrected click block logic:

```javascript
joinBtn.addEventListener("click" , () => {
    // 1. Increment data
    streamSong.activeListeners += 1;
    // 2. Sync UI Text
    streamCount.textContent = streamSong.activeListeners;

    // 3. Evaluate state
    if (streamSong.activeListeners > 0) {
        songCard.classList.remove("empty-stream");
    } else {
        songCard.classList.add("empty-stream");
    }
});
```

