-now tell me what can be done just suggest me ÇHere is the cleanest architectural roadmap to fix Project 6 using your preferred workflow pattern (checking the click target $\rightarrow$ updating state $\rightarrow$ rendering HTML).

---

### Step 1: Use Root-Level Event Delegation
Instead of looping over `.btn` with `querySelectorAll`, place **one** click listener on the container (`#catalog-container` or `.container`). This completely fixes the `button.btn.cart` crash.

```javascript
document.querySelector(".container").addEventListener("click", (e) => {
    // Check if what was clicked is an "add to cart" button
    const cartBtn = e.target.closest(".cart");
    
    if (cartBtn) {
        extraction(cartBtn);
    }
});
```

---

### Step 2: Fix `extraction()` to Pass a String
Walk up to `.item-row`, pull the `<h3>` text content, and pass the string to `checking()`.

```javascript
const extraction = (letsFind) => {
    let parentCard = letsFind.parentElement;
    let heading = parentCard.querySelector("h3");
    checking(heading.textContent.trim());
};
```

---

### Step 3: Fix `checking()` to Push Objects (Not Strings)
Find the full product object in `catalog`. Check if it's already in `carte` before pushing, so you track quantity instead of creating duplicates.

```javascript
const checking = (itemsWanted) => {
    // 1. Find the full product object in catalog
    const foundProduct = catalog.find(item => item.name === itemsWanted);
    if (!foundProduct) return;

    // 2. Check if product is already in carte
    const existingInCart = carte.find(item => item.name === itemsWanted);

    if (existingInCart) {
        existingInCart.quantity += 1;
    } else {
        carte.push({ ...foundProduct, quantity: 1 });
    }

    // 3. Trigger cart render
    addingHTML(carte);
};
```

---

### Step 4: Fix `addingHTML()` (Clear Container + Calculate Totals)
Clear `cartContainer.innerHTML = ""` at the start of the function to prevent exponential DOM duplication, draw the items, and calculate subtotal/tax/total.

```javascript
const addingHTML = (checkingOut) => {
    // Clear container to avoid duplicate appending
    cartContainer.innerHTML = "";

    let subtotal = 0;

    checkingOut.forEach((checking) => {
        let newElement = document.createElement("div");
        newElement.classList.add("item-row");
        
        // Multiply price by quantity
        const itemTotal = checking.price * checking.quantity;
        subtotal += itemTotal;

        newElement.innerHTML = `
            <h3>${checking.name} (x${checking.quantity})</h3>
            <p>$${itemTotal.toFixed(2)}</p>
        `;
        cartContainer.appendChild(newElement);
    });

    // Update Summary UI
    const tax = subtotal * 0.08;
    const grandTotal = subtotal + tax;

    document.getElementById("subtotal").textContent = `$${subtotal.toFixed(2)}`;
    document.getElementById("tax").textContent = `$${tax.toFixed(2)}`;
    document.getElementById("grand-total").textContent = `$${grandTotal.toFixed(2)}`;
};
```

---

