---

### How to Fix `checking()`

Rewrite `checking()` so it handles all 3 states cleanly[cite: 7]:

```javascript
const checking = (itemsWanted, stat) => {
    const foundProduct = catalog.find(item => item.name === itemsWanted);
    if (!foundProduct) return;

    const existingInCart = carte.find(item => item.name === itemsWanted);

    if (stat === "cart" || stat === "add") {
        if (existingInCart) {
            existingInCart.quantity += 1;
        } else {
            carte.push({ ...foundProduct, quantity: 1 });
        }
    } else if (stat === "minus") {
        if (existingInCart) {
            existingInCart.quantity -= 1;
            // Remove item from cart completely if qty reaches 0
            if (existingInCart.quantity <= 0) {
                carte = carte.filter(item => item.name !== itemsWanted);
            }
        }
    }

    addingHTML(carte);
}
```

And update your event listener so it only runs when an actual button is clicked[cite: 7]:

