### How to Fix `checking()`

You don't actually need to calculate and store `checkOutValue` inside each object! You can compute totals dynamically inside `calculation()`. 

If you want to keep `checkOutValue`, fix the initial addition like this:

```javascript
const checking = (itemsWanted, stat) => {
    const foundProduct = catalog.find(item => item.name === itemsWanted);
    if (!foundProduct) return;

    const existingInCart = carte.find(item => item.name === itemsWanted);

    if (!existingInCart) {
        // Initial push: quantity 1, price * 1
        carte.push({ 
            ...foundProduct, 
            quantity: 1, 
            checkOutValue: foundProduct.price 
        });
    } else if (stat === "cart" || stat === "add") {
        existingInCart.quantity += 1;
        existingInCart.checkOutValue = existingInCart.quantity * existingInCart.price;
    } else if (stat === "minus" && existingInCart.quantity >= 1) {
        existingInCart.quantity -= 1;
        existingInCart.checkOutValue = existingInCart.quantity * existingInCart.price;
        
        // Cleanup if quantity reaches 0
        if (existingInCart.quantity === 0) {
            carte = carte.filter(item => item.name !== itemsWanted);
        }
    }

    addingHTML(carte);
}
```∆
