now i want to do project 7 É3Welcome to **Project 7: Multi-Criteria Filter Engine & Search Engine**! 

Having completed the Cart Engine in Project 6, you've mastered state array mutations (`push`, `filter`, updating object properties) and syncing that array to the DOM.

In Project 7, you'll tackle a crucial architectural concept: **Data Querying & Derived UI State**.

---

### The Goal of Project 7

Build a fast, interactive product filter interface. Users should be able to:
1. Type into a text input to **search products by name**.
2. Click category tags (e.g., *All, Electronics, Accessories, Clothing*) to **filter by category**.
3. Use a range slider or select input to **filter by max price**.
4. Combine all three filters simultaneously without resetting the others.

---

### Key Architectural Concepts You'll Practice

* **The Single Source of Truth:** Your main dataset array never changes. You do not mutate `catalog`.
* **Derived State / Pipeline Pattern:** Instead of modifying data, you create a pipeline function (e.g., `getFilteredProducts()`) that passes `catalog` through three checks:
  $$\text{Catalog} \xrightarrow{\text{Search}} \text{Filtered 1} \xrightarrow{\text{Category}} \text{Filtered 2} \xrightarrow{\text{Price}} \text{Render Target}$$
* **Debouncing / Input Events:** Handling continuous keyboard events smoothly without thrashing the DOM.

---

