## 5. How You'll Implement It in Project 9

In Project 9 (a Persistent Shopping Cart & Preferences App), you will write logic that looks like this:

1. **Read on Startup:**
   ```javascript
   // Fallback operator (||) guarantees we default to [] if localStorage is empty
   const cart = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("cart")) || [];
   ```
2. **Sync on Action:**
   Every time a user clicks "Add to Cart", "Delete", or toggles "Night Mode", you will update the state array and immediately save it to storage:
   ```javascript
   function saveCart() {
       localStorage.setItem("cart", JSON.stringify(cart));
   }
   ```

