ﬁcan i make a website that i functional like i want to make  a simple responsive website. I wanted to ask before that is this a huge concept e.g., showing a "Loading products..." spinner before the network request returns)?˚Not at all! A loading spinner is actually a **very simple concept**‚Äîit sounds fancy, but under the hood, it‚Äôs literally just **toggling a element's visibility** before and after your `await fetch()` call.

Here is the exact mental model for how it works:

1. **Before fetching:** Show a spinner (or text like "Loading products...") in your HTML.
2. **`await fetch(...)` runs:** The code pauses while waiting for the API.
3. **After data arrives:** Hide or replace the spinner with your rendered products.

It usually takes less than 5 lines of code:

```javascript
const getProductsFromAPI = async () => {
    // 1. Show loading state in the UI
    productList.innerHTML = "<p>Loading products...</p>";

    try {
        const response = await fetch('https://dummyjson.com/products?limit=8');
        const data = await response.json();
        
        // 2. Clear loading text & render real data
        productList.innerHTML = ""; 
        visualisation(data.products);
    } catch (error) {
        productList.innerHTML = "<p>Failed to load products.</p>";
    }
};
```

