          <p className="text-slate-400 text-sm">@alex_dev</p>
        </div>

        {/* DYNAMIC FOLLOW BUTTON */}
        <button
          onClick={() => setIsFollowing(!isFollowing)}
          className={`px-4 py-2 rounded-xl text-sm font-semibold transition-all duration-200 active:scale-95 ${
            isFollowing
              ? 'bg-slate-800 text-slate-300 border border-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-750'
              : 'bg-indigo-600 text-white hover:bg-indigo-500 shadow-lg shadow-indigo-600/30'
          }`}
        >
          {isFollowing ? 'Following' : 'Follow'}
        </button>

      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

---

### What to Notice Here

* **Dynamic Class Name Switching:** Look at the button's `className`. We used a JS template literal (`` `...` ``) combined with a ternary operator (`isFollowing ? '...' : '...'`) to swap background and text colors instantly.
* **Flexbox Layout:** `flex items-center gap-4` on the card container aligns the avatar, info, and button horizontally with equal 16px (`gap-4`) spacing.
* **Micro-Interactions:** `active:scale-95` creates a natural button-press animation without writing `@keyframes` CSS.

